  "title": "codex turn.failed: no turn.completed is emitted, so no usage exists",
  "handWritten": true,
  "notARecording": "Hand-written from the documented codex exec JSONL event shapes and the documented fact that a failed turn emits turn.failed and never turn.completed. No CLI was executed to produce this file.",
  "spec": "docs/spec/usage-normalization.md",
  "scenario": {
    "backend": "github-actions",
    "runtime": "codex",
    "authMode": "subscription-login",
    "runId": "run_01JQ8ZF0Y2Z5B8E1G4J7M0Q3S9",
    "cycleIndex": 3,
    "nodeId": "code-review",
    "attempt": 1,
    "sessionPolicy": "fresh",
    "note": "The turn ran, consumed quota, and then failed. The runtime emits no usage for a failed turn, so the record is unavailable. Failure classification (this message classifies as QUOTA and drives WAITING_FOR_QUOTA) is a separate concern from usage and must not be allowed to invent a usage number."
  },
